            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0399" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.0144/13</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 840</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department invites attention to the
                    fact that it has received up to the present no reply whatever to its
                    instructions No. 643, September 12, 1922, and No. 781, January 18, 1923, on the
                    subject of Wrangell Island. Please report immediately concerning the steps which
                    have been taken in this matter and the results obtained.</p>
                <p>In this connection you are informed that the Department is advised by the
                    Secretary of War that a map of the world recently published by the Department of
                    the Interior of Canada shows Wrangell Island as a British possession.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William
                            Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
